  "previous_increment": "doc/validation/bounded-native-state-copy-2026-09-13.json",
  "behavior": [
    "HostSlotTable directly owns an actual boxed extent; its separate metadata token contains no pointer to elements and cannot grant source-data access.",
    "Cold attachment and retirement serialize without locking hot mutable values. Retirement fences new attachments before payload destruction; elements and charge destructors run outside locks. Escaped tokens conservatively retain earlier charges.",
    "DeviceState and native key/value, hybrid layer and hybrid fixed-role storage preserve borrowed access, numerical clone semantics and existing replacement-versus-reuse behavior while giving real new tables independent identities.",
    "Native inventory includes exact table identity and inline capacity through required state visitors. Initial and final operation publication attach actual source charges before relinquishing existing authority. Partial publication preserves prior attachments and source authority or quarantine.",
    "Dormant hybrid prediction prototypes contribute their actual shared layout and layer/fixed tables alongside independently deduplicated native storage.",
    "Loaded Llama and Qwen fixtures verify complete initial publication. DeepSeek V4 retains Unknown/loading authority for lazy rotary helper copies; only its known table inventory is separately published under that authority for the source-lifetime test.",
    "Exchange tests preserve the original table charge when it moves into a saved state, until that saved state or its final accounting token retires."
  ],
  "initial_findings": [
    "Staged test compile errors included two obsolete SharedStorageDomain constructors, a missed mutable slice access, and a missing RuntimeStateComponents import; corrected.",
    "An attention-backed prototype cannot call advance_fixed; its attention append already advances its frontier. Removed the invalid call.",
